From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 182] panvk: optional dump of tiler heap descriptor state
Generated-by: LLM

Debug only: with PANVK_HEAP_TRACE=1, every 64 fragment submissions log
the completed top/bottom range stored by the command stream at fragment
finish, the whole tiler context and the active TILER_HEAP descriptor, to check whether the hardware
reports the chunk range that fragment finish should release. biblioklept

The dump now waits for all iteration scoreboards first, so it cannot race the
tiler write-back (biblioklept).

It also copies the firmware heap context (free list head and counters) at
each fragment CALL and prints the whole 64-byte descriptor slot.

Also dumped: the header of the current and of the first heap chunk, and the
tiler context as the vertex-tiler side sees it after FINISH_TILING.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/181

